// Keybindings shared by the repositories that use this tooling.
//
// Why this exists: the mypy editor extension re-checks when you type, when you
// save, or when a tracked setting changes - but NOT when a file changes on
// disk from outside the editor. Edits made by a formatter, sed or an agent tool
// therefore leave stale diagnostics in the Problems panel.
//
// VERIFYING THIS CHORD ACTUALLY WORKS
// ====================================
// Do not assume a binding is live just because it is in this file. A `when`
// clause that is false silently disables the chord - VS Code reports nothing,
// and the key simply appears dead.
//
// That is what happened here. This binding shipped with:
//
//     "when": "editorTextFocus || terminalFocus"
//
// which looks harmless but is exactly backwards for its purpose. Someone with
// stale errors is reading the PROBLEMS PANEL, so focus is not in the editor
// and not in the terminal, both clauses are false, and Ctrl+Shift+Alt+M does
// nothing at all. The one situation this escape hatch exists for was the one
// situation it could not be triggered from.
//
// Hence: NO `when` clause below. An emergency recovery key must fire
// unconditionally, from any focus context - editor, Problems panel, SCM,
// terminal, Explorer. If a future key genuinely cannot be unconditional, give
// it its own chord rather than narrowing this one.
//
// A keybinding only conflicts visibly in Ctrl+K Ctrl+S (search the chord); a
// false `when` clause will NOT show up there as a conflict.
//
// Fallback when even this does not fire: Ctrl+Shift+P -> "restart" ->
// the mypy entry. Or just run, from the repo root:
//
//     uv run python .github/scripts/refresh_editor_types.py
//
// which nudges the tracked setting that prompts the re-check and needs no
// keybinding at all. Note the explicit `uv run python`: this repository has
// no bare `python` on PATH, so the script must be invoked through the venv.
[
  {
    "key": "ctrl+shift+alt+m",
    "command": "mypy-type-checker.restart"
  },
  {
    "key": "cmd+shift+alt+m",
    "command": "mypy-type-checker.restart",
    "when": "isMac"
  }
]
